{
  "description": "Synthetic cases of the masking of the views served by Mothra (mothra-slices task 15.3): the primary rule, the pairs and the series rule of the lead time and throughput view, the statistics masked with their headcount, the shares masked with their part, their whole and their rest. Invented teams A and B, invented counts, no real data. Each case gives rows (a column left out is NULL), the columns judged (`cells`) and the [row index, column] pairs expected to be masked once every rule is applied. The columns of a view are those of contrats/vues.json. Source of the rules: tools/flow_views.py (masquer_vue); players: the npm suite (mothra/contract/test/masquage.test.ts) and the Python suite (tests/flow_views/test_cas_vues_tranche1.py). A masked count, statistic or share is a masked cell for both players (the statistics and shares are the `maskableColumns` of contrats/vues.json, R-20261030-49).",
